<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26758" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lĭquāmen</span></b> ,
			ĭnis, n.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				liquid mixture</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eo liquamine tonsa ovis imbuitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					7, 4, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A sauce</i> made of fish-fat, <i>fish-sauce</i> (cf. garum), <i><span class="en">Col. 6, 2,
			7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pall. 3, 25,
			12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> =
			lixivium, <i>lye</i>, <i><span class="en">Cael.
				Aur. Tard. 2, 13, 167</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
